    {
      "id": "evidence-000-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Both steps are definitional in the normalized ofNat/negSucc representation -- `ofNat n + 1` iota-reduces to `ofNat (succ n)`, `0 + (-1)` to `negSucc 0`, and `negSucc n + (-1)` to `negSucc (succ n)` -- so each branch is `Nat.rec` applied to the hypotheses with no rewriting. Two `Weakening` variants replace the +1 and the -1 step with `True`; the kernel refuses this declaration in both cases.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "733126c0f351f0931f7eaf0b4f5f9f569f3aef44",
          "source": "commit",
          "unix": 1787338967
